        <groundspeak:log id="684644985">
          <groundspeak:date>2017-05-06T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="946600">Black Shark</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP722 Mill Creek Ravine South&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our first cap in Edmonton on our &quot;all caps, all day&quot; trip.  Have to wonder if people living across from cap placements like this one notice visitors to the cap and if they go out afterwards and find what people are looking at and scratch their heads at the photography sessions?  Of course, with a flush with the ground cap like this they would have to be lucky to look out at just the right time because the visits are short.  We didn't notice anyone outside or at windows in our moments here. A nice verdigris cap with scuffs around the &lt;em&gt;edges&lt;/em&gt; which removed many letters but left the numbers readable.  Thanks for the cap.&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="683865764">
